dzn: Only name the depth and stencil planes an image has

Applications name stencil for a depth-only image, or depth for a
stencil-only one, in barriers and clears, which other Vulkan drivers ignore.
Dozen made planes and clear flags of whatever aspects the application
named. A barrier on the second plane of a single-plane texture is not a
valid D3D12 subresource range: D3D12 refused to close the command list
(E_INVALIDARG), and executing it removed the device
(DXGI_ERROR_INVALID_CALL). Destiny Rising clears its D32_SFLOAT shadow map
with both aspects, so under WSL2 it crashed 18 to 35 s after every launch,
in Venus and gfxstream_guest_angle mode alike, and took every other app
drawing with the GPU, or in gfxstream mode the whole VM, with it.

dzn_image_aspects() keeps the depth and stencil aspects the image's format
has. The internal barriers before clears and loads, vkCmdPipelineBarrier2
(in its counting pass as in the one that fills the barriers, so the two
agree), the legacy barrier path and the depth/stencil clears use it, and
skip a barrier or a clear left with nothing. A stencil-only barrier from
vkCmdPipelineBarrier2 now names plane 1, as the internal ones do, instead
of the depth plane.

